{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovNormalized","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.PresentedGroup"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup.braidTrace_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup.braidTrace_one","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidGroup.lean#L150-L155","doc":"The trace of the trivial braid is `1` — the normalisation, restated on braids. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup.braidTrace_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup.braidTrace_conj","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidGroup.lean#L138-L148","doc":"**Markov move I, on braids.** The trace is a conjugation invariant of the braid, so it is\nalready constant on the conjugacy classes that move I identifies.\n\nThis is `markovTr_mul_comm` transported through the representation; the representation being a\n*group* hom is what lets `γ⁻¹` appear at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup.braidTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup.braidTrace","kind":"def","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidGroup.lean#L130-L136","doc":"**The normalised Markov trace of a braid**: represent it in `H_{m+1}(q)`, then take the\nnormalised site-weighted trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup.heckeRep_braidGen_val","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup.heckeRep_braidGen_val","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidGroup.lean#L119-L124","doc":"The value of a generator in the algebra, not the unit group. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup.heckeRep_braidGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup.heckeRep_braidGen","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidGroup.lean#L115-L117","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup.heckeRep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup.heckeRep","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidGroup.lean#L103-L113","doc":"**The braid representation** `Art(M) → H(M, q²)ˣ`, `σ_i ↦ σ_i`.\n\nThe universal property of the presentation does all the work: the only obligation is the braid\nrelation in the unit group, and `σ_i` is a unit because it satisfies the §7a quadratic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup.sigmaUnit_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup.sigmaUnit_braid","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidGroup.lean#L94-L101","doc":"**The braid relation holds among the `σ_i` as units.** `Balanced.sigma_braid` pushed along\n`Units.coeHom`; nothing is re-derived. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup.val_altProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup.val_altProd","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidGroup.lean#L88-L92","doc":"`altProd` of units is computed in the group and then coerced — `map_altProd` along\n`Units.coeHom`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup.BraidGroupN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup.BraidGroupN","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidGroup.lean#L80-L82","doc":"**The braid group on `m+1` strands**, as the Artin group of the type-`A` Coxeter matrix\nalready used by `heckeActionN`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup.braidGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup.braidGen","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidGroup.lean#L77-L78","doc":"The `i`-th Artin generator `σ_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup.ArtinGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup.ArtinGroup","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidGroup.lean#L73-L75","doc":"**The Artin group** of `M` — the braid group of the corresponding Coxeter system. Mathlib\nhas no braid group, so this is built from `PresentedGroup`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup.artinRels","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup.artinRels","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidGroup.lean#L64-L71","doc":"**The Artin relations** of a Coxeter matrix `M`: for each pair `i, j`, the alternating word\n`i j i ⋯` of length `M i j` equals `j i j ⋯` of length `M j i`.\n\nWritten with the same `altProd` as the Hecke algebra's braid relation, so the two are one\nstatement in two monoids. ","signatureChunk":0}]}